  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Summary\n\nValtuutus 2.2.1 fixes the cached latest snap token moving backwards under concurrent writes.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- **Caching:** concurrent offers of the latest snap token could land an older token last, so requests without a snap token read at a snapshot that missed writes already announced through  (#347, closes #346).\n  - Each process now keeps the newest token it has seen per cache and never reads below it.\n  - Within one process, a request without a token now reads at the newest announced token or later.\n  - Across nodes sharing a distributed cache, a request without a token is not guaranteed to see a write announced on another node. Pass the snap token  returns for read-your-writes there.\n\n## Pull requests\n\n- #347 fix(caching): keep the latest snap token from moving backwards",
